# Compiled example binaries.
#
# `go build` / `go run`-leftover outputs are named after the example's leaf
# directory. Depending on where `go build` is invoked they land either in
# examples/go/ or in the example's own subdirectory (e.g.
# events/wildcard-subscribe/wildcard-subscribe). These are extension-less
# Mach-O / ELF files the repo-root .gitignore's *.exe / *.dylib rules do NOT
# catch. The patterns below are intentionally unanchored so each known example
# binary is ignored at any depth.
ack-and-redelivery
auth-jwt
basic-pubsub
command-round-trip
mqtt-v311-vs-v5
query-round-trip
shared-consume
start-new-only
tls
websocket
wildcard-subscribe
